/ACROSS PAGES AND ARE IMPORTANT.

WATFLG,	-1		/SET TO THE CHARACTER WAITING FOR IF THE COMMAND IS IN
			/PROCESS.  IT IS LOOKED ON BY DISK AND HOST JOBS.
DBCHRP,	0		/CONTAINS THE CURRENT ADDRESS IN THE BUFFER OPENED
DBCHRC,	0		/CONTAINS THE -LIMIT CNTR FOR THE BUFFER OPEN BY DBFINI.
DBRCHP,	0		/CONTAINS A PNTR TO THE CURRENT ADDRS ON THE RECV BUFFER
DBRCHC,	0		/MAX SIZE OF THE BUFFER
SNDFLG,	0		/SET TO 1 IF THERE IS A BUFFER THAT HAS TO BE SENT NOW.
TESTFL,	0		/IF 1 THEN DISPLAY ALL ERROR MESSAGES
ERRFLG,	0		/IS SET TO 1 ON THE FIRST ERROR DISCOVERED
DGTTM1,	0		/POINTER USED BY DGTARG FOR THE POINTER TO THE NEXT ARG
			/ALSO MOVED BY GETASC WHEN IN AN ASCII STRING
